; active-inference.fk — a prediction-relation organ: predict -> observe -> mismatch -> update offer.
;
; The body predicts the next thing; the world delivers what actually happened; their relation is witnessed.
; A mismatch (predicted != actual) is SURPRISE and offers a place where the model may bend. A match is
; confirmation: it does not request that bend, but it remains evidence and may still teach in the larger
; learning relation. This cell measures that narrow prediction relation. It does not govern curiosity,
; minimize surprise as a way of life, or decide which inquiry matters most.
;
; This COMPOSES sequence-predictor: there the body PREDICTS the next symbol (sp-predict). Here we name the
; other half of the loop explicitly — the witnessed prediction relation. A step is (list predicted actual): predicted is what
; sp-predict (or any predictor) said, actual is what the stream then delivered. A run is a list of steps.
; The surprise-count over a run is the total prediction-mismatch count — the same evidence-counting spine as
; sequence-predictor's sp-followers-count and classifier-eval's hit-count, walked over (predicted,actual)
; pairs instead of adjacent symbols. Strings, so the match is str_eq (eq is for ints/nodes).
;
; Honest lane: surprise is never fabricated low. A miss is a miss; ai-surprise-count counts every one, and
; ai-settled? gates only this predictor's residual fit (ge tolerance surprises). "Settled" here means the
; predictor fits this witnessed run within tolerance, not that the field is exhausted or inquiry should
; cease. tolerance 0 demands a perfect run; nothing is rounded toward "settled." Counts are integers 0..N.
;
; `ai-learn?` is retained as the narrow "model-bend offered?" compatibility surface. It does not claim that
; matching steps teach nothing. `attuned-surprise-inquiry.fk` composes both matches and mismatches into the
; inquiry braid and witnesses executed movement as learning in either case.
;
; Proven by: form-stdlib/tests/active-inference-band.fk (four-way at validate.sh, incl. fkwu)

(do
    ; --- HIT: the prediction landed. predicted == actual -> 1, else 0. ---
    ; step is (list predicted actual); nth 0 is the prediction, nth 1 is what the world delivered.
    (defn ai-hit? (step)
        (if (str_eq (nth step 0) (nth step 1)) 1 0))

    ; --- SURPRISE: the inverse of a hit. A miss (predicted != actual) IS a surprise -> 1, else 0. ---
    ; Computed from the same str_eq, not by negating ai-hit?'s integer — keeps the 1/0 honest in every kernel.
    (defn ai-surprised? (step)
        (if (str_eq (nth step 0) (nth step 1)) 0 1))

    ; --- MODEL-BEND OFFER (legacy name): surprise asks this predictor to update. ---
    ; A matching step confirms this predictor and does not ask it to bend. The larger learning organ still
    ; keeps both outcomes; ai-learn? is the historical compatibility name for this narrower update request.
    (defn ai-learn? (step)
        (ai-surprised? step))

    ; --- SURPRISE-COUNT: total prediction error over the run = how many steps missed. ---
    ; Walk the steps, +1 (the step's surprise) each; the same evidence-counting spine as sp-followers-count.
    (defn ai-surprise-count (run)
        (if (eq (len run) 0) 0
            (add (ai-surprised? (head run)) (ai-surprise-count (tail run)))))

    ; --- HIT-COUNT: how many steps landed = the evidence the model already fits. ---
    (defn ai-hit-count (run)
        (if (eq (len run) 0) 0
            (add (ai-hit? (head run)) (ai-hit-count (tail run)))))

    ; --- SETTLED: this predictor fits the witnessed run within the supplied residual tolerance. ---
    ; (ge tolerance surprises) -> 1 = fit; else 0 = still bending. This is not a command to stop inquiry.
    ; tolerance 0 demands a flawless run; nothing rounds toward settled. Same ge-gate as classifier-eval's accept.
    (defn ai-settled? (run tolerance)
        (if (ge tolerance (ai-surprise-count run)) 1 0))

    0)
